quran[12]{c,v,t}:
  25,44,"Do you think that most of them listen or understand? They are just like cattle. Instead, they are further astray from the (right) way."
  25,45,"Have you not considered how your Lord extends the shade (till noon)? Had He willed, He could have made it (remain) stationary. Then We made the sun an indicator over it."
  25,46,"Then, We withdraw it towards Ourselves, drawing little by little."
  25,47,And He is the One Who made the night for you as a covering and sleep as a (means of) rest. And He made the day for rising again (so that you may earn a livelihood).
  25,48,"And He is the One Who sends the winds as good news heralding His mercy. And We send down from the sky purifying water,"
  25,49,so that We may revive a dead land with it and provide it as a drink to many of the cattle and humans We have created.
  25,50,"Indeed, We distribute it among them so they may be mindful of advice. But most people refuse (to be anything) but ungrateful."
  25,51,"Had We wished, We would have certainly raised a warner in every town."
  25,52,"So do not obey the disbelievers, but strive against them a great striving through this (Qur’an)."
  25,53,"And He is the One Who has merged the two seas: this one sweet and fresh, and that one salty and bitter. And between the two, He has made a barrier and a forbidden hindrance."
  25,54,"He is the One Who created the human being from water, then made him kin with ties of blood and marriage. And your Lord is All-Capable."
  25,55,"Yet they worship (things) besides Allah, which can neither benefit them nor cause them harm. And the disbeliever is always a helper (of Satan) against his Lord(’s command)."
